        <register>
          <name>CQRS14</name>
          <description>CQRS14 - Task Clear
 S/W writes 1 to N bit of this register to clear task N. Bit remains 1 until clear operation is completed. Once operations ends, the CQE clears this bit to 0. The S/W has to ensure the CQ Engine is halted before clearing tasks. The S/W can clear only single task. When any bit of this register is set, the S/W has no to request new task clear. This operation clears only task in the Host Controller. The S/W should take care about clearing task in the device.
 Writing 0 to register is ignored.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x438</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>CQTC31</name>
              <description>CQTC31 - Command Queuing Task Clear #31</description>
              <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CQTC30</name>
              <description>CQTC30 - Command Queuing Task Clear #30</description>
              <bitRange>[30:30]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CQTC29</name>
              <description>CQTC29 - Command Queuing Task Clear #29</description>
              <bitRange>[29:29]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CQTC28</name>
              <description>CQTC28 - Command Queuing Task Clear #28</description>
              <bitRange>[28:28]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
